{"kind":"github_issue","repository":"microsoft/vscode-copilot-release","item":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836/events","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836","id":3158842782,"node_id":"I_kwDOJYd5Dc68SB2e","number":12836,"title":"Add Model Specification in `prompt.md` Files","user":{"login":"beingminimal","id":84431724,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDMxNzI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84431724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal","html_url":"https://github.com/beingminimal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-06-19T04:05:40Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T20:26:54Z","closed_at":"2025-12-12T20:26:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nCurrently, `prompt.md` files lack the ability to specify a **custom model name**, forcing all prompts to rely on a default model configuration. This limits prompt precision and power, as complex prompts requiring advanced reasoning cannot be reliably configured, while simpler prompts might unnecessarily consume more powerful (and expensive) models.\n\n\n## Solution\n\nIntroduce a `model` property in the `prompt.md` frontmatter. This allows users to explicitly define the AI model to be used for the prompt's execution, creating more powerful, self-contained, and predictable automations.\n\n**Example `prompt.md`:**\n\n```markdown\n---\nmode: 'agent'\nmodel: 'gpt-4.1'\ndescription: 'Generate a new React form component'\n---\nYour goal is to generate a new React form component based on the templates in #githubRepo contoso/react-templates.\n\nAsk for the form name and fields if not provided.\n\nRequirements for the form:\n* Use form design system components: [design-system/Form.md](../docs/design-system/Form.md)\n* Use `react-hook-form` for form state management:\n* Always define TypeScript types for your form data\n* Prefer *uncontrolled* components using register\n* Use `defaultValues` to prevent unnecessary rerenders\n* Use `yup` for validation:\n* Create reusable validation schemas in separate files\n* Use TypeScript types to ensure type safety\n* Customize UX-friendly validation rules\n```\n\n## Benefits\n\n* **Precision and Power:** Assign specific models like `claude-sonnet-4` or `gemini-2.5-pro` for tasks requiring particular capabilities, ensuring optimal performance and accuracy.\n* **Cost and Performance Optimization:** Match the model's capability to the task's complexity, ensuring efficient resource utilization and faster responses for simpler prompts.\n* **Workflow Automation:** Create robust, one-click workflows that reliably execute multi-step tasks with the correct model, increasing developer productivity.","closed_by":{"login":"bhavyaus","id":25044782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDQ0Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25044782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus","html_url":"https://github.com/bhavyaus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned","pinned_comment":null},"comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2986749575","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836#issuecomment-2986749575","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12836","id":2986749575,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yBi6H","user":{"login":"sascharo","id":88222654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MjIyNjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88222654?v=4","grava